<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cadwallon ap Cadfan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 634</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Cadwallon of Gwynedd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cadwallon ap Cadfan was a king of Gwynedd who, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>, defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edwin-of-northumbria">Edwin of Northumbria</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hatfield-chase">Battle of Hatfield Chase</a> in 633. He then ravaged Northumbria for a year, killing Edwin's successors Osric and Eanfrith, until Oswald defeated and killed him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-heavenfield">Battle of Heavenfield</a> in 634. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> portrayed him as a cruel tyrant.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cadwallon-ap-cadfan.jpg" alt="Cadwallon ap Cadfan" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cadwallon_ap_Cadfan_Peniarth_MS_23C_(f.99.v)_transparency.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
